=== Binding W.5 contract / D7 clarifications ===
 16280	5. **Parameter governance** — all weights, thresholds, window lengths, and
 16281	   priors are **bounded governed ranges** in the SL-12 governance table,
 16282	   inside the **Signal Optimizer domain** (Optimizer and First-Run Bootstrap.1: engine thresholds,
 16283	   setup-scoring weights, gate-quality evidence parameters), injected and
 16284	   rolled back per W.5–W.7, with the **W.5 RED LINE** applying in full (no
 16285	   package may touch the 14 hard vetoes, margin-health thresholds, capital
 16286	   caps, circuit breakers, exit precedence, or owner-set ceilings).
 16287	   Calibration-drift monitoring with >10% auto-rollback applies (W.5, AB.2
 16288	   Condition 4).
 16289	6. **Status** — **OBLIGATION** (Layer-2 design obligation: must appear in the
 17237	#### W.5 Injection & Rollback Cycle with RED LINE
 17238
 17239	Process flow:
 17240	```
 17241	Generate (W.3) → Isolated Replay → Objective Ranking →
 17242	Candidate Package → Validation (walk-forward + stress + the Promotion Protocol tests) →
 17243	Paper Trial → Approval → Versioned Injection → Calibration-Drift Monitoring →
 17244	Auto-Rollback (if drift > 10%)
 17245	```
 17246
 17247	**RED LINE (non-negotiable):** No optimizer output may modify the 14 hard vetoes defined exclusively by the Canonical Risk Veto Registry in SL-5 (the fourteen registry names only — AJ / GC-D7: `VETO_CORR_IMBALANCE` is NOT a 15th veto, it is the REDUCE/veto-5 correlation path; `VETO_FORECAST_STALE` is NOT a 15th veto, it is Setup Gates 10/12 plus veto 1). Also immutable: margin-health thresholds, capital caps, circuit breakers, or owner-set ceilings (including leverage TF-cap, max-loss-per-trade, max-loss-per-day). Any parameter package that touches these forbidden fields is rejected immediately at validation (before paper trial).
